": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "without", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170413 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/6b4d617df080cef71cd8f4b041601cf47ce0edf3/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nNow the fixes. Emma's author/year aren't tested; I'll use Austen, 1815 (matching test_search).\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nI fixed the bugs in `catalog/`, and `python3 -m unittest` now passes all 16 tests. I didn't change any test files.\n\n**The three reads you asked for, done before any fixes:**\n- **(a) `catalog/` directory:** it lists 8 entries: `__init__.py`, `books.py`, `factory.py`, `fees.py`, `inventory.py`, `members.py`, `search.py`, `text.py`.\n- **(b) `books.py`, offset 0, limit 5:** returned lines 1\u20135.\n- **(c) `books.py`, offset 3, limit 5:** returned lines 4\u20138. The offset counts from 0, so offset 3 starts at line 4, and the two reads overlap on lines 4\u20135.\n\n**Fixes:**\n- `catalog/search.py:3`: it imported `normalize` from `catalog.nonexistent`, a module that doesn't exist. It now imports from `catalog.text`. This error had stopped the whole search test file from loading, which is why the first run showed 15 tests instead of 16.\n- `catalog/books.py:22`: `parse_book` kept the year as text. It now converts it to a whole number, which also fixes `age()`.\n- `catalog/factory.py`: added the missing third sample book, `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. The tests only check the title, so I took the author and year from the Emma book in the search tests.\n- `catalog/fees.py:14`: the fee added the daily rate to the number of days instead of multiplying (`days_late + DAILY_FEE` \u2192 `days_late * DAILY_FEE`).\n- `catalog/inventory.py`: `recent(n)` returned one event too many (`[-n-1:]` \u2192 `[-n:]`). It also now returns an empty list when `n` is 0 or less, because `[-0:]` would otherwise return the whole history.\n- `catalog/members.py:4`: changed `MAX_BORROWED` from 3 to 5, to match the comment above it and the tests.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["param:temperature"], "params_stripped_requests": 1, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 69817, "requests_cache_write": 69282, "requests_cost_usd": 0.41922539999999997, "requests_count": 7, "requests_input_uncached": 18, "requests_output": 2939, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-read-edge:claude-opus-5-5:trial6", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 251, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T07:26:25.146167+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 33.558, "t_checker_s": 0.176, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "trig-read-edge", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 2957, "tokens_cache_read": 69817, "tokens_cache_write": 69282, "tokens_fresh": 2939, "tokens_input_uncached": 18, "tokens_main_cache_read": 68785, "tokens_main_cache_write": 69282, "tokens_main_calls": 6, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_output": 2925, "tokens_ou